From 1a272088d97cb328b65762ceea63906cd8ca2a5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:34:42 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 41/48] GE: draw line and line-strip primitives as quads one
 PSP pixel wide

Lines were skipped. Each segment now becomes two triangles through the
draw's own pipeline (blending, depth, stencil, masks), so no new topology:
one PSP pixel wide along the minor axis (the coverage of the GE's line, so
an additive line adds the same light per length and keeps its width at any
internal scale), no caps (a strip's shared end is not drawn twice), colour,
texture coordinates and depth per end. Transformed segments are cut at the
near plane and their corners handed back in object space, as transformed
sprites are, so frame interpolation blends them like any other draw.
Through-mode segments are centred half a pixel in, the pixel a coordinate
names. Culling is off for lines.

<prefix>_NO_LINES skips lines as before; <prefix>_TRACE_LINES[=N] logs line
draws and per-frame counts. The census counts lines as drawn
(prim.lines_drawn) unless the switch is set. Tests in render_tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
